 <paragraph index="100" node_type="writer">Introduction</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="102" node_type="writer">This part of the project is to explain the installation and the configuration of all the software needed for the project; before doing this, I will check my computer specification to know if it can support the software.</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="107" node_type="writer">I- MY COMPUTER SPECIFICATIONS</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="109" node_type="writer">1-To check my ram: free -h</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="110" node_type="writer">It means I have a total memory of 14 GB and 6.9 GB is free. The RAM is the memory used by the computer to perform operations, and it’s sufficient for this project.

2-To see the GPU: lspci | grep -i vga</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="111" node_type="writer">It means the GPU is an AMD/ATI Barcelo (Radeon integrated).

3- To see my ubuntu version:  lsb_release -a</paragraph>
 <paragraph index="112" node_type="writer">This Ubuntu version is too recent for ROS Noetic used for this project. ROS Noetic need Ubuntu 24. </paragraph>
 <paragraph index="115" node_type="writer">4-To check the disk space: df -h /

</paragraph>
